            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 516)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Optimized media can no longer be encoded without a colour config.</b> <code>Asobi optimize</code> used to carry on when it had no OCIO config — encoding with no log curve at all, then writing "ACES - ACEScct" into the sidecar anyway and reporting success. The stand-in looked plausible and played back wrong, and nothing downstream could tell, because the sidecar itself was the thing that was lying. It now stops and says so. Pre-renders on a nominated machine are where this hid, since nothing there has a window to show a warning in.</li>
<li><b>A stand-in's sidecar always tells the truth about its colour now.</b> The shaper it records is decided by whether a transform actually ran, not by what was asked for — so no future caller can reintroduce the same mismatch.</li>
<li><b>Session packages fail loudly instead of quietly.</b> A shot whose stand-in can't be built correctly — a config with no route from the source space to the shaper — now packs its frames and tells you why, rather than travelling as a movie that never went through the curve its sidecar names. A package is the thing that leaves the building, so it is the worst place to be silently wrong.</li>
<li><b>New <code>--no-color</code> flag</b> for the deliberate no-colour-management case. The sidecar then records no shaper, so playback doesn't undo a curve that was never applied.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
